message:
Now I see the issue clearly. In `each_backtrace`:

```c
if (mrb->c->cibase[i].pc) {
    pc = &mrb->c->cibase[i].pc[-1];
}
else {
    continue;
}
idx = (uint32_t)(pc - irep->iseq);
mrb_debug_get_position(mrb, irep, idx, &loc.lineno, &loc.filename);
```

If `ci->pc` points to one past the end of the iseq, then `pc = ci->pc - 1` points to the last instruction, and `idx = irep->ilen - 1`, which is `< irep->ilen`. So `mrb_debug_get_position` should succeed.

But wait - what if `ci->pc` is NULL? Then it would `continue`. But what if `ci->pc` points to a position that's beyond the iseq by more than 1?

Actually, let me re-read the `mrb_debug_get_position` function:

<｜｜DSML｜｜>
<parameter=command>grep -n "mrb_debug_get_position" /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/mruby/src/debug.c</｜｜DSML｜｜>
</｜｜DSML｜｜>

